{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794597201,"nonce":"ZGUpARZ+XgSuQIrlAughVHjK8jU=","message":"Implementing the remaining typed-stream failure gap as Stream\u003cResult\u003cT, E\u003e\u003e, where T is any supported stream value and E names a #[hxn::data] error implementing Display. Haxe sees hxn.Stream\u003cT\u003e; the first Err ends the read side and becomes the generated exception, after preceding Ok values. Queued values after the error are released outside the queue lock and subsequent sends are refused. Existing Sender::fail failures retain their status/message/payload.\n\nThe safe AnyStream::next_result method converts errors on the taking thread and closes before invoking the generated converter. No hxn-abi implementation, layout, dependency or runtime export changed; hxn-future gains no unsafe. The generator records the carried result in the manifest, collects stream-only error types, separates take names by value/error, retains implicit element exports for object batches, and wraps stream failures on Haxe as futures already do. Core/generator tests cover the transport, terminal cleanup, reentrant drops, racing producers, type/shape errors and collisions. Runtime checks cover scalar/data/unit/bytes/object/optional/batch streams, listen, and one-shot error consumption. The pantry example takes an order and reports its first typed error after earlier items.\n\nInitial generated HashLink and hxcpp fixtures pass. Full runtime, NUC, Miri and mobile validation is beginning. Uncommitted, not pushed. The completed cooperative-Miri issue was committed separately as 7d7dae2.","files":null}]}